# Mutation: `emit()` never sets EVENT_FLAG_PATH_TRUNCATED. Rebuilding the bpf
# ELF is required for this one; `run.sh` does it.
#
# Must fail: `a_truncated_docker_sock_path_still_kills_and_says_the_match_was_asserted`,
# at the one assertion in that file which reads the raw record flag rather than
# what the agent made of it. That assertion exists because a silent fallback is
# a defect waiting for the next producer that has no fallback.
#
# This header said, for one cycle, that the patch survived on purpose. It does
# not, and never did: measured on Linux 6.18.44 with the harness beside it, the
# join reports `FAILED. 3 passed; 1 failed`, panicking at the one `assert!` on
# `Event::path_truncated()`.
# Nothing had run the harness; the claim came from reading `Event::flags` and
# from a separate hand-run, and it was wrong in both directions.
#
# The property it was reaching for is real. Cycle 8 closed the fail-open twice —
# `emit()` sets the flag from the length it read, and `ferrum_ebpf::path_truncated`
# derives the same answer from the bytes that arrived, so an ELF predating the
# fix cannot fail open. The second half is what covers a pre-fix object, and
# this patch still cannot measure it: the raw-flag assertion runs *before* the
# verdict assertions in that test, so with this patch applied the run stops at
# that assertion and never reaches the kill, the `path_unknown` or the SIGKILL
# it would have to observe to make the claim.
#
# That is what `05-decoder-trusts-the-truncation-flag.patch` is for. It comes at
# the same property from the consumer's side, against a test that takes the
# over-long record *this kernel wrote* and clears the one bit in the bytes, so
# the derivation is what decides and deleting it is visible as a verdict rather
# than as a flag assertion. The two patches are not redundant: this one says the
# datapath still flags what it could not carry, that one says a producer which
# never learned to is still covered.
diff --git a/crates/ferrum-ebpf-progs/src/main.rs b/crates/ferrum-ebpf-progs/src/main.rs
index fe1cdd4..d741930 100644
--- a/crates/ferrum-ebpf-progs/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/ferrum-ebpf-progs/src/main.rs
@@ -130,9 +130,9 @@ mod progs {
                 Ok(len) => len < PATH_LEN - 1,
                 Err(_) => false,
             };
-            if !fits {
-                event.flags |= EVENT_FLAG_PATH_TRUNCATED;
-            }
+            // MUTATION: a path the helper could not carry whole is recorded
+            // as if it had arrived intact.
+            let _ = fits;
         }
         match FERRUM_EVENTS.reserve::<Event>(0) {
             Some(mut slot) => {
